on` or metrics yet. The estimates are marked `[model]`.\n- **Body:** all nine sections in order, 749 words (the limit is 800). Every claim is tagged `[model]`.\n- **Available oracle:** this is the input PKT-0002 needs. The tests call only five `utils.js` functions directly: `downloadUrlPromise`, `postRequestPromise`, `encryptPassword`, `decryptPassword` and `watchWithFallback`. Four internal helpers are covered indirectly. I listed 26 untested functions that need no fakes (the best first targets) and about 25 that would need fake requests, connections, files or network. `httpRequest` has no tests at all.\n\n## Decisions\n- **Entry points:** ranked by counting `require` calls across the repo. The top three are `operationContext` (32), `utils` (31) and `commondefines` (21).\n- **Two files I left alone:**\n  - I did not edit `INDEX.md`; the spec says it is generated, not edited by hand.\n  - I did not append to `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl`. It is outside `create_in`, and this run's rules allow writes only there.\n\n  Both entries are below so you or the factory can add them.\n- **Executor log:** written here only, because the packet file is under `.theseus/queue/`, which I was told not to edit.\n\n## Lessons for the Atlas\n- The modules load each other in a loop: `utils` → `operationContext` → `tenantManager`/`runtimeConfigManager` → `utils`. The order they load in matters.\n- Loading `utils.js` changes global objects: it adds `BigInt.prototype.toJSON` and `Date.prototype.addMonths`, and calls `win-ca`. Tests need `NODE_CONFIG_DIR` set, which `tests/env-setup.js` does.\n- `ctx.getCfg` returns only the static default until `initTenantCache()` has run. Per-tenant settings are silently ignored before that.\n- The queue transport (RabbitMQ or ActiveMQ) is fixed once, when the module loads.\n- `checkPathTraversal` only checks for null bytes and a `startsWith` prefix, so callers must pass an already-resolved path.\n- Three open questions are in the card (is ActiveMQ used, which callers pass unresolved paths, should `utils.js` be split). Each could become an `investigate` packet; I created none.\n\n## Friction to record\n1. The executor prompt and `AGENTS.md` say to append to `friction.jsonl` and fill in the packet's \"Executor log\", but the run rules forbid both locations. One of them should change.\n2. The acceptance commands (`theseus validate`) and the commit both needed approval the run didn't have, so the executor can't prove or deliver the packet on its own.\n3. The packet doesn't say whether `INDEX.md` should be regenerated; `max_files_changed: 2` hints that it should.","ttft_ms":3474,"type":"result","duration_ms":172542,"uuid":"d6624912-24ad-40ad-b8dc-d2343f4b4d27","ttft_stream_ms":2029,"time_to_request_ms":370,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":203,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":21,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":7,"engine_pickup":9,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":20,"query_setup":6,"auto_mode_context_wait":22,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":32,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":6,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":75,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":199,"time_to_request_major_faults":34,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":216,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":142,"process_rss_mib_result":238,"process_anon_mib_result":146,"process_peak_rss_mib":252,"process_cpu_ms_turn":4987,"process_wall_ms_turn":172542,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":2267,"process_wall_ms_streaming":114552,"main_stream_count":33,"main_stream_event_count":1933,"main_stream_chunk_count":1385,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":8,"cpu_ms":21,"major_faults":2,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":8,"ambient_wait_ms":8,"rend